KG42.register("rules-dc48eadfe863881ecd9486ec",{"id":"37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R004","paper":"37-dsm_auction_incentives","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The power distribution company renews the electricity price used to coordinate users' price-responsive consumption decisions. Scope: Periodic DSM operation cycles, under the stated assumption that users shift consumption in response to electricity prices.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e08"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Periodic DSM operation cycles, under the stated assumption that users shift consumption in response to electricity prices.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e08"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The power distribution company renews the electricity price used to coordinate users' price-responsive consumption decisions. Scope: Periodic DSM operation cycles, under the stated assumption that users shift consumption in response to electricity prices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d83df5b2d1-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. System Model / A. DSM Scenario in the SG","anchor_text":"II, same way, different types of users gain different utilities (levels he of satisfaction). the Sma","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Power Distribution Company: The power distribution company periodically collect users' consumption demand, optimize the next-operation-cycle load allocations, renew the electricity price, and deliver the optimal consumption plans and electricity bills to all users. For data security, the power distribution company keeps a copy of each user's historical demand declarations and consumption information."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-d83df5b2d1-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. System Model / A. DSM Scenario in the SG","anchor_text":"consumption of user in time slot . We deﬁne as the vector of energy consump- tion of user . We deﬁne","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"3) Consumption Boundary: We set consumption boundaries for each time slot, considering the conditions such as there are appliances that have to be always on, which causes must-run loads [20], and there exists power limitation. In time slot s, let B_i^s and b_i^s denote the maximum and minimum consumption limits for user i, respectively. We make \\mathbf{B}_i \\triangleq (B_i^1,B_i^2,\\ldots,B_i^S) and \\mathbf{b}_i \\triangleq (b_i^1,b_i^2,\\ldots,b_i^S) denote the maximum and minimum consumption limits for user i in all time slots, respectively. 4) Feasible Consumption: Let x_i^s denote the power consumption of user i in time slot s. We define \\mathbf{x}_i \\triangleq (x_i^1,x_i^2,\\ldots,x_i^S) as the vector of energy consumption of user i. We define X_i \\triangleq \\{\\mathbf{x}_i \\mid b_i^s \\le x_i^s \\le B_i^s, \\forall s \\in \\mathcal{S}\\} to be user i's feasible energy consumption set. As in [3], we also assume that user would like to shift their energy consumption in response to the price values [21]-[23]."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No source-supported design or operational variable is defined for this rule in the supplied evidence. The cited text describes the procedural act of renewing an electricity price but does not define a typed decision variable, domain, or unit, and the frozen graph contains no variable node for this relation.","empty_theta_reason":"No source-supported parameter is defined for this rule in the supplied evidence. The cited text gives neither a fixed price coefficient, a price formula, nor parameter values associated with coordination.price_signal, and the frozen graph contains no parameter node for this relation."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","quote":"The power distribution company periodically collect users' consumption demand, optimize the next-operation-cycle load allocations, renew the electricity price, and deliver the optimal consumption plans and electricity bills to all users."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e08","quote":"As in [3], we also assume that user would like to shift their energy consumption in response to the price values [21]-[23]."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"851cdd3503c9855cbff7de06948dde544197021b46f502890d40fd6a7078f672","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule expresses a procedural coordination relation: the power distribution company periodically renews the electricity price, and users are assumed to shift consumption in response to price values. The supplied candidate evidence for this rule describes the renewal action and the behavioral assumption but does not define a price-setting formula, a typed price decision variable, or a parameter tied to the two frozen nodes. Therefore no mathematical expression can be transcribed without inventing one; the existing core constraint remains not_formalized. B evidence is unreviewed candidate support, not independently verified source correctness.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The constraint binds the distribution-company coordination node to the price-signal node through the frozen links edge. Evidence e06 describes the company renewing the electricity price during periodic DSM operation, and e08 states the assumption that users shift consumption in response to price values. The relation is procedural and is recorded without a mathematical expression because the supplied evidence does not give a price formula or typed variable definitions for these nodes."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
